refkv_embed.js and refkv_ir.wasm are built from refkv
(https://github.com/d-v-b/refkv) commit 18d72f8d (branch feat/grib,
d-v-b/refkv#166), MIT OR Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-MIT here; Apache-2.0 is
Neuroglancer's own license):

    just js::wasm          # rust/refkv-ir as refkv_ir.wasm (wasm32)
    node js/build.mjs      # js/src/embed.ts bundled as refkv_embed.js

and copied from refkv's js/dist/ unchanged. refkv_embed.js is refkv's
zarrifier for a host that reads the input itself (js/src/embed.ts): it
zarrifies a file through the host's reads, or a store at an http(s) URL, with
refkv's Rust core (refkv_ir.wasm), and writes a vzip archive; and it decodes the
refkv.fits_tiles and refkv.grib codecs' chunks with the same core. The refkv:
kvstore (src/kvstore/refkv/) and the refkv.fits_tiles and refkv.grib codecs
(src/datasource/zarr/codec/refkv_fits_tiles/ and refkv_grib/) use it through
core.ts, which finds the wasm module. refkv_embed.d.ts declares its API.
